{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 825 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "7ff5327f7e3e5eb02124c1b6ffe24d94e9634781d8ab08522f1d0c66bffc521e" :edb/db-before-t 824 :edb/db-after-t 825 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534137 50 #inst "2026-10-11T16:59:24.067Z" 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186203683 1071 "Consider the following set:\n\n$$\nA = \\big\\{\\mathbb{Z}, \\mathbb{Q}, \\mathbb{R}\\big\\}\n$$\n\nGiven the relation $R$ on $A$ defined by\n\n$$\nX\\:R\\: Y \\quad \\Leftrightarrow \\quad \\mathbb{Q} \\subseteq X \\cap Y,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $\\mathbb{Z} \\: R \\: \\mathbb{Q}$\n\n- $\\mathbb{R} \\: R \\: \\mathbb{R}$\n\n- $\\mathbb{Q} \\: \\cancel{\\!R\\!}\\: \\mathbb{R}$" 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186203683 1071 "Consider the following set:\n$A = \\big\\{\\mathbb{Z}, \\mathbb{Q}, \\mathbb{R}\\big\\}$\n\nGiven the relation $R$ on $A$ defined by\n$X\\:R\\: Y \\quad \\Leftrightarrow \\quad \\mathbb{Q} \\subseteq X \\cap Y$,\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $\\mathbb{Z} \\: R \\: \\mathbb{Q}$\n2. $\\mathbb{R} \\: R \\: \\mathbb{R}$\n3. $\\mathbb{Q} \\: \\cancel{\\!R\\!}\\: \\mathbb{R}$" 13194139534137 17592186045417 false] [17592186203683 1074 "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product\n\n$$\nA\\times A = A^2\n$$\n\n$R\\subseteq A^2$\n\nWe also have the following notations:\n\n- $x \\: R \\: y$ if and only if $(x,y) \\in R$\n- $x \\: \\require{cancel}\\cancel{\\!R\\!} \\: y$ if and only if $(x,y) \\notin R$\n\nIn this case, we have $X \\: R \\: Y$ if and only if $\\mathbb{Q} \\subseteq X \\cap Y$.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. In this case, we have $\\mathbb{Q} \\subseteq \\mathbb{Z} \\cap \\mathbb{Q}$, which is false.\n- Statement II is true. In this case, we have $\\mathbb{Q} \\subseteq \\mathbb{R} \\cap \\mathbb{R}$, which is true.\n- Statement III is false. In this case, we have $\\mathbb{Q} \\not\\subseteq \\mathbb{Q} \\cap \\mathbb{R}$, which is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139534137 17592186045417 false] [17592186203683 1074 "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A = A^2.$\n\n$$\nR\\subseteq A^2\n$$\n\nWe also have the following notations:\n\n- $x \\: R \\: y$ if and only if $(x,y) \\in R$\n\n- $x \\: \\require{cancel}\\cancel{\\!R\\!} \\: y$ if and only if $(x,y) \\notin R$\n\nIn this case, we have $X \\: R \\: Y$ if and only if $\\mathbb{Q} \\subseteq X \\cap Y.$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. In this case, we have $\\mathbb{Q} \\subseteq \\mathbb{Z} \\cap \\mathbb{Q},$ which is false.\n\n- Statement II is true. In this case, we have $\\mathbb{Q} \\subseteq \\mathbb{R} \\cap \\mathbb{R},$ which is true.\n\n- Statement III is false. In this case, we have $\\mathbb{Q} \\not\\subseteq \\mathbb{Q} \\cap \\mathbb{R},$ which is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186203691 1071 "Let $A = \\mathbb{R}$, and consider the relation $R$ on $A$ such that $x \\: R \\: y$ if and only if $x$ and $y$ both lie above the upward-opening parabola whose focus is at $\\left(0,\\dfrac14\\right)$ and whose vertex is at $O$. Express $R$ using set-builder notation." 13194139534137 17592186045417 false] [17592186203691 1071 "Let $A = \\mathbb{R},$ and consider the relation $R$ on $A$ such that $x \\: R \\: y$ if and only if $x$ and $y$ both lie above the upward-opening parabola whose focus is at $\\left(0,\\dfrac14\\right)$ and whose vertex is at $O.$ Express $R$ using set-builder notation." 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186203691 1074 "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product\n\n$$\nA\\times A = A^2\n$$\n\n$$\nR\\subseteq A\\times A\n$$\n\nFor a relation $R$ on a set $A$, we also have the following notations:\n\n- $a \\: R \\: b$ if and only if $(a,b) \\in R$\n- $a \\: \\cancel{\\!R\\!} \\: b$ if and only if $(a,b) \\notin R$\n\nIn this case, $R$ is the set of ordered pairs\n\n$$\n(x,y) \\in \\mathbb{R} \\times \\mathbb{R} = \\mathbb{R}^2\n$$\n\nsuch that $y \\gt x^2$.\n\n![](images/26/26671c4dc03b13afc43172e486602bf3d647f8be911769c24a9e0523f591b64b.png)\n\nTherefore, we can write out $R$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\nR = \\Big\\{(x,y) \\in \\mathbb{R}^2 \\:: \\: y \\gt x^2 \\Big\\}\n$$" 13194139534137 17592186045417 false] [17592186203691 1074 "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A = A^2.$\n\n$$\nR\\subseteq A\\times A\n$$\n\nFor a relation $R$ on a set $A,$ we also have the following notations:\n\n- $a \\: R \\: b$ if and only if $(a,b) \\in R$\n\n- $a \\: \\cancel{\\!R\\!} \\: b$ if and only if $(a,b) \\notin R$\n\nIn this case, $R$ is the set of ordered pairs $(x,y) \\in \\mathbb{R} \\times \\mathbb{R} = \\mathbb{R}^2$ such that $y \\gt x^2.$\n\n![](images/26/26671c4dc03b13afc43172e486602bf3d647f8be911769c24a9e0523f591b64b.png)\n\nTherefore, we can write out $R$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\nR = \\Big\\{ (x,y) \\in \\mathbb{R}^2 \\: : \\: y \\gt x^2 \\Big\\}\n$$" 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186203695 1071 "Consider the following set:\n\n$$\nA = \\big\\{\\mathbb{R}_0^+, \\mathbb{R}_0^-, \\mathbb{R}\\big\\}\n$$\n\nGiven the relation $R$ on $A$ defined by\n\n$$\nX\\:R\\: Y \\quad \\Leftrightarrow \\quad X\\supset Y,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $\\mathbb{R} \\: R\\: \\mathbb{R}_0^-$\n\n- $\\mathbb{R}_0^- \\: R\\: \\mathbb{R}_0^+$\n\n- $\\mathbb{R}_0^+ \\: \\cancel{\\!R\\!} \\: \\mathbb{R}$" 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186203695 1071 "Consider the following set:\n$A = \\big\\{\\mathbb{R}_0^+, \\mathbb{R}_0^-, \\mathbb{R}\\big\\}$\n\nGiven the relation $R$ on $A$ defined by\n$X\\:R\\: Y \\quad \\Leftrightarrow \\quad X\\supset Y$,\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $\\mathbb{R} \\: R\\: \\mathbb{R}_0^-$\n2. $\\mathbb{R}_0^- \\: R\\: \\mathbb{R}_0^+$\n3. $\\mathbb{R}_0^+ \\: \\cancel{\\!R\\!} \\: \\mathbb{R}$" 13194139534137 17592186045417 false] [17592186203695 1074 "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product\n\n$$\nA\\times A = A^2\n$$\n\n$R\\subseteq A^2$\n\nWe also have the following notations:\n\n- $x \\: R \\: y$ if and only if $(x,y) \\in R$\n- $x \\: \\require{cancel}\\cancel{\\!R\\!} \\: y$ if and only if $(x,y) \\notin R$\n\nIn this case, we have $X \\: R \\: Y$ if and only if $X\\supset Y$. For this relation, note that\n\n- the symbols $R$ and $\\supset$ are interchangeable, and\n- the symbols $\\cancel{\\!R\\!}$ and $\\not\\supset$ are also interchangeable.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Replacing $R$ with the symbol $\\supset$, we have $\\mathbb{R} \\supset \\mathbb{R}_0^-$. This is equivalent to $\\mathbb{R}_0^- \\subset \\mathbb{R}$, which is true.\n- Statement II is false. Replacing $R$ with the symbol $\\supset$, we have $\\mathbb{R}_0^- \\supset \\mathbb{R}_0^+$. This is equivalent to $\\mathbb{R}_0^+ \\subset \\mathbb{R}_0^-$, which is false.\n- Statement III is true. Replacing $\\cancel{\\!R\\!}$ with the symbol $\\not\\supset$, we have $\\mathbb{R}_0^+ \\not\\supset \\mathbb{R}$. This is equivalent to $\\mathbb{R} \\not\\subset \\mathbb{R}_0^+$, which is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139534137 17592186045417 false] [17592186203695 1074 "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A = A^2.$\n\n$$\nR\\subseteq A^2\n$$\n\nWe also have the following notations:\n\n- $x \\: R \\: y$ if and only if $(x,y) \\in R$\n\n- $x \\: \\require{cancel}\\cancel{\\!R\\!} \\: y$ if and only if $(x,y) \\notin R$\n\nIn this case, we have $X \\: R \\: Y$ if and only if $X\\supset Y.$ For this relation, note that\n\n- the symbols $R$ and $\\supset$ are interchangeable, and\n\n- the symbols $\\cancel{\\!R\\!}$ and $\\not\\supset$ are also interchangeable.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Replacing $R$ with the symbol $\\supset,$ we have $\\mathbb{R} \\supset \\mathbb{R}_0^-.$ This is equivalent to $\\mathbb{R}_0^- \\subset \\mathbb{R},$ which is true.\n\n- Statement II is false. Replacing $R$ with the symbol $\\supset,$ we have $\\mathbb{R}_0^- \\supset \\mathbb{R}_0^+.$ This is equivalent to $\\mathbb{R}_0^+ \\subset \\mathbb{R}_0^-,$ which is false.\n\n- Statement III is true. Replacing $\\cancel{\\!R\\!}$ with the symbol $\\not\\supset,$ we have $\\mathbb{R}_0^+ \\not\\supset \\mathbb{R}.$ This is equivalent to $\\mathbb{R} \\not\\subset \\mathbb{R}_0^+,$ which is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186203899 1038 #edb/ref 17592186411677 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186203899 1038 #edb/ref 17592186411678 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186203900 1038 #edb/ref 17592186411679 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186203901 1038 #edb/ref 17592186411680 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186204118 1050 480.0 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186204239 1068 #edb/ref 17592186200122 13194139534137 17592186045417 false] [17592186204239 1068 #edb/ref 17592186200127 13194139534137 17592186045417 false] [17592186204239 1068 #edb/ref 17592186200133 13194139534137 17592186045417 false] [17592186204239 1068 #edb/ref 17592186411667 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186204239 1068 #edb/ref 17592186411672 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186204239 1068 #edb/ref 17592186411675 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186204239 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186204239 1071 "Let $A = R$, and consider the relation \"greater than or equal to\" on $A$. Express the relation using set-builder notation.$x \\le y$ {{field-1}} {{field-2}} {{field-3}}" 13194139534137 17592186045417 false] [17592186204239 1071 "Let $A=R,$ and consider the relation \"greater than or equal to\" on $A.$ Express the relation using set-builder notation." 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186204239 1074 "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A={A}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR⊆A\\times A\n$$\n\nFor a relation $R$ on a set $A,$ we also have the following notations:\n\n- $a\\,R\\,b$ if and only if $(a,b)\\in R$\n\n- $a\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,b$ if and only if $(a,b)\\notin R$\n\nIn this case, $R$ is the set of ordered pairs $(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}$ such that $x\\ge y.$\n\nTherefore, we can write out $R$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\nR={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,x\\ge y}\n$$" 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186204623 1068 #edb/ref 17592186203626 13194139534137 17592186045417 false] [17592186204623 1068 #edb/ref 17592186411674 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186204623 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186204623 1071 "Given the relation $R$ on $Z$ defined by\n\n$$\nx\\,R\\,y\\,⇔\\,x∣(y-1),\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $4\\,R\\,13$\n- $3\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,11$\n- $8\\,R\\,3$" 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186204623 1071 "Given the relation $R$ on $Z$ defined by\n\n$xRy⇔x∣(y - 1)$,\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $4R13$\n2. $3R11$\n3. $8R3$" 13194139534137 17592186045417 false] [17592186204623 1074 "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A={A}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR⊆A\\times A\n$$\n\nWe also have the following notations:\n\n- $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\in R$\n\n- $x\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\notin R$\n\nIn this case, we have $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $x∣(y-1).$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. In this case, we have $4∣(13-1),$ which is true.\n\n- Statement II is true. In this case, we have $3∤(11-1),$ which is true.\n\n- Statement III is false. In this case, we have $8∣(3-1),$ which is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186205236 1064 "Recall that a binary relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product\n\n$$\nA\\times A = A^2{:}\n$$\n\n$$\nR\\subseteq A^2\n$$\n\nAdditionally, we have the following notations:\n\n- $x \\: R \\: y$ if and only if $(x,y) \\in R$\n- $\\require{cancel}x \\: \\cancel{\\!R\\!} \\: y$ if and only if $(x,y) \\notin R$\n\nRelations can be defined over infinite sets. For example, consider the relation $R$ on $\\mathbb{Z}$ defined by\n\n$$\nx \\: R \\: y \\qquad \\Leftrightarrow \\qquad x \\geq y\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $x \\: R \\: y$ if and only if\n\n$$\nx \\geq y\n$$\n\nFor this relation, note that\n\n- the symbols $R$ and $\\geq$ are interchangeable, and\n- the symbols $\\cancel{\\!R\\!}$ and $\\not\\geq$ (or, equivalently, $\\cancel{\\!R\\!}$ and $\\lt$) are also interchangeable.\n\nFor example:\n\n- $2 \\: R \\: 0$ since $2 \\geq 0$\n- $\\require{cancel} 1 \\: \\cancel{\\!R\\!} \\: \\pi$ since $1 \\not\\geq \\pi$\n- $0 \\: R \\: 0$ since $0 \\geq 0$\n\nFinally, since $R$ is the set of ordered pairs $(x,y) \\in \\mathbb{Z}^2$ such that\n\n$$\nx \\geq y\n$$\n\nwe can write out $R$ in set-builder notation as\n\n$$\nR = \\big\\{(x,y) \\in \\mathbb{Z}^2 \\:: \\: x \\geq y \\big\\}\n$$" 13194139534137 17592186045417 false] [17592186205236 1064 "Recall that a binary relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A = A^2{:}$\n\n$$\nR\\subseteq A^2\n$$\n\nAdditionally, we have the following notations:\n\n- $x \\: R \\: y$ if and only if $(x,y) \\in R$\n\n- $\\require{cancel}x \\: \\cancel{\\!R\\!} \\: y$ if and only if $(x,y) \\notin R$\n\nRelations can be defined over infinite sets. For example, consider the relation $R$ on $\\mathbb{Z}$ defined by\n\n$$\nx \\: R \\: y \\qquad \\Leftrightarrow \\qquad x \\geq y.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $x \\: R \\: y$ if and only if $x \\geq y.$ For this relation, note that\n\n- the symbols $R$ and $\\geq$ are interchangeable, and\n\n- the symbols $\\cancel{\\!R\\!}$ and $\\not\\geq$ (or, equivalently, $\\cancel{\\!R\\!}$ and $\\lt$) are also interchangeable.\n\nFor example:\n\n- $2 \\: R \\: 0$ since $2 \\geq 0$\n\n- $\\require{cancel} 1 \\: \\cancel{\\!R\\!} \\: \\pi$ since $1 \\not\\geq \\pi$\n\n- $0 \\: R \\: 0$ since $0 \\geq 0$\n\nFinally, since $R$ is the set of ordered pairs $(x,y) \\in \\mathbb{Z}^2$ such that $x \\geq y,$ we can write out $R$ in set-builder notation as \n\n$$\nR = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\in \\mathbb{Z}^2 \\: : \\: x \\geq y \\big\\}.\n$$" 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186411621 1080 "1" 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186411621 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186411621 1083 #uuid "04b7cd61-6d77-5fba-b3b8-52a35ad4aff7" 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186411622 1080 "II only" 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186411622 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186411622 1083 #uuid "08f7679f-73f5-5a0e-a03f-dee0f63f3f77" 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186411623 1080 "{R}^{2}" 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186411623 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186411623 1083 #uuid "0e6adea3-006c-533e-a33c-0dfacf799aac" 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186411624 1080 "R" 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186411624 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186411624 1083 #uuid "1acafbe5-6096-5090-b29d-42eefc9ae48b" 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186411625 1080 "(x,y)" 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186411625 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186411625 1083 #uuid "1b24f77e-0b5e-5992-aab2-7c2712cb6787" 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186411626 1080 "II only" 13194139534137 17592186045417 