 $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\in R$\n\n- $x\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\notin R$\n\nIn this case, we have $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $x>y.$ For this relation, note that\n\n- the symbols $R$ and $>$ are interchangeable, and\n\n- the symbols $\\cancel{\\,R\\,}$ and $≯$ (or, equivalently, $\\cancel{\\,R\\,}$ and $\\le $) are also interchangeable.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. Replacing $R$ with the symbol $>,$ we have $6>8,$ which is false.\n\n- Statement II is true. Replacing $R$ with the symbol $>,$ we have $7>2,$ which is true.\n\n- Statement III is false. Replacing $\\cancel{\\,R\\,}$ with the symbol $\\le ,$ we have $9\\le 1,$ which is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186411678 1068 #edb/ref 17592186411670 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186411678 1069 "q-212926" 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186411678 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186411678 1071 "Given the relation $R$ on $Z$ defined by\n\n$$\nx\\,R\\,y\\,⇔\\,x∣y,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $6\\,R\\,3$\n- $5\\,R\\,8$\n- $7\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,9$" 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186411678 1072 #uuid "a8c98d98-74bc-5116-9f06-75c38fdcf981" 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186411678 1074 "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A={A}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR⊆A\\times A\n$$\n\nWe also have the following notations:\n\n- $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\in R$\n\n- $x\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\notin R$\n\nIn this case, we have $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $x∣y.$ For this relation, note that\n\n- the symbols $R$ and $∣$ are interchangeable, and\n\n- the symbols $\\cancel{\\,R\\,}$ and $∤$ are also interchangeable.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. Replacing $R$ with the symbol $∣,$ we have $6∣3,$ which is false.\n\n- Statement II is false. Replacing $R$ with the symbol $∣,$ we have $5∣8,$ which is false.\n\n- Statement III is true. Replacing $\\cancel{\\,R\\,}$ with the symbol $∤,$ we have $7∤9,$ which is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186411679 1068 #edb/ref 17592186411673 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186411679 1069 "q-212983" 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186411679 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186411679 1071 "Given the relation $R$ on $Z$ defined by\n\n$$\nx\\,R\\,y\\,⇔\\,x≡y+4\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6),\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $0\\,R\\,2$\n- $1\\,R\\,9$\n- $4\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,13$" 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186411679 1072 #uuid "b5b2a52b-fd77-5422-b1dc-3a9ca690060e" 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186411679 1074 "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A={A}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR⊆A\\times A\n$$\n\nWe also have the following notations:\n\n- $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\in R$\n\n- $x\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\notin R$\n\nIn this case, we have $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $x≡y+4\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6),$ or equivalently, $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $6∣(x-y-4).$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. In this case, we have $6∣(0-2-4),$ which is true.\n\n- Statement II is true. In this case, we have $6∣(1-9-4),$ which is true.\n\n- Statement III is true. In this case, we have $6∤(4-13-4),$ which is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186411680 1068 #edb/ref 17592186411669 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186411680 1068 #edb/ref 17592186411671 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186411680 1068 #edb/ref 17592186411676 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186411680 1069 "q-218358" 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186411680 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186411680 1071 "Let $A=Z,$ and consider the relation $R$ on $A$ such that $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $3\\,|\\,(x+y).$ Express $R$ using set-builder notation." 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186411680 1072 #uuid "e2674a53-8856-5a0e-8ea3-7bef241518ca" 13194139534137 17592186045417 true] [17592186411680 1074 "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A={A}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR⊆A\\times A\n$$\n\nFor a relation $R$ on a set $A,$ we also have the following notations:\n\n- $a\\,R\\,b$ if and only if $(a,b)\\in R$\n\n- $a\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,b$ if and only if $(a,b)\\notin R$\n\nIn this case, $R$ is the set of ordered pairs $(x,y)\\in Z\\times Z={Z}^{2}$ such that $3\\,|\\,(x+y).$\n\nTherefore, we can write out $R$ in set-builder notation as follows:\n\n$$\nR={(x,y)\\in {Z}^{2}\\,:\\,3\\,|\\,(x+y)}\n$$" 13194139534137 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-04b7cd61-6d77-5fba-b3b8-52a35ad4aff7" 17592186411621 "answer-08f7679f-73f5-5a0e-a03f-dee0f63f3f77" 17592186411622 "answer-0e6adea3-006c-533e-a33c-0dfacf799aac" 17592186411623 "answer-1acafbe5-6096-5090-b29d-42eefc9ae48b" 17592186411624 "answer-1b24f77e-0b5e-5992-aab2-7c2712cb6787" 17592186411625 "answer-1f17869c-0ece-5ef7-a77d-d4d3abc9fe0f" 17592186411626 "answer-24ec285a-89b6-5e80-85cf-547592c0be93" 17592186411627 "answer-29192154-5fca-5c4c-ba05-c1677c12f786" 17592186411628 "answer-2ddca7f1-da8d-5b3b-a8af-f028a712c9a2" 17592186411629 "answer-316794dc-dda4-5deb-8016-1610db41a730" 17592186411630 "answer-31da6476-a086-5047-92af-0b7f80a9e936" 17592186411631 "answer-322a920c-999f-5ebf-b81b-f1fdff28d7f6" 17592186411632 "answer-3e90ef8b-8d7b-59de-9f36-95572e6e5a15" 17592186411633 "answer-3f926afe-f465-5842-9bd3-aad8b7d5dc0e" 17592186411634 "answer-3fc0e208-9604-504a-95ef-5c18fe697075" 17592186411635 "answer-47f66e07-d1c0-5f79-82e3-fcb796015fd1" 